/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"FINAL - Cabinet Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50984/final-cabinet-treasury-management-outturn-report-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"14/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50827/treasury-management-outturn-report-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Audit","date":"24/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Statement of Accounts Audit Committee","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50855/statement-of-accounts-audit-committee.pdf","committee":"Audit","date":"24/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Dacorum Draft Statement of Accounts 202526","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50880/dacorum-draft-statement-of-accounts-202526.pdf","committee":"Audit","date":"24/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"OSC Financial Monitoring Outturn 2025.26","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50779/osc-financial-monitoring-outturn-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","date":"17/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix D Capital Outturn","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50783/appendix-d-capital-outturn.pdf","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","date":"17/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"MTFS 2026-2031 Report","url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s50778/mtfs-2026-2031-report.pdf","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","date":"17/06/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Strategic Planning & Environment Overview & Scrutiny","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Housing and Community Overview and Scrutiny","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-11","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-01","committee":"Strategic Planning & Environment Overview & Scrutiny","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Audit","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Housing and Community Overview and Scrutiny","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Dacorum housing depot project \u00a31.5m over budget as capital delivery falters","lead":"Dacorum council faces a \u00a31.5m overspend on the Paradise Depot, a housing repairs scheme budgeted at \u00a37.2m but now projected to cost \u00a38.7m \u2014 a 21% overspend and the largest single capital overspend in the entire programme. Work is well underway with nearly \u00a31m already spent. The overspend comes as the council's housing investment programme more broadly stutters: a scheme to build new council homes budgeted at \u00a34.4m is now forecast to spend only \u00a31m this year, a 77 per cent shortfall. Meanwhile, the council has discovered the Forum's electricity meter was faulty for years; repair work completed in April means annual utility bills will jump by \u00a3200k. The findings emerged from the Finance and Resources scrutiny committee's review of quarter-one spending.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Appendix D","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51278/51278.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Dacorum housing projects face \u00a31.5m cost overrun and major delays","lead":"Dacorum's housing investment programme is under strain, with the Paradise Depot refurbishment 21 per cent over budget at \u00a31.5m and spending already accelerating, the council's finance scrutiny committee heard. The council budgeted \u00a37.2m for the project but now expects to spend \u00a38.7m. Separately, the HRA New Properties programme, allocated \u00a34.4m to build new council housing, is forecast to spend only \u00a31m this year \u2014 a 77 per cent shortfall with no spending recorded to date. A new community facility at The Hub also faces a \u00a3180k overspend. The slippage suggests either delay in planning permission or procurement, while the Paradise Depot overrun reflects rising costs already being incurred.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Appendix D","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51278/51278.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Dacorum housing scheme slips \u00a33.4m while Paradise Depot overruns by \u00a31.5m","lead":"Dacorum's housing revenue account\u2014the council's account for its own homes, funded by rents\u2014faces significant delivery problems. The HRA New Properties scheme, allocated \u00a34.4m for new homes, is forecast to spend only \u00a31m this year, a 77 per cent shortfall with no spending to date indicating major delays or scope reduction. Paradise Depot, budgeted at \u00a37.2m, is projected to cost \u00a38.7m\u2014a \u00a31.5m overrun which the council's quarterly monitoring identifies as the largest single cost overrun in the entire capital programme, despite \u00a3926k already spent. General Fund building and assets projects also report \u00a32.1m underspending against a budget of \u00a313.7m.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Appendix D","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51278/51278.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","paper_title":"Appendix G","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51281/51281.pdf","headline":"HRA financing costs ratio swings sharply from 22.20% to -21.90% between budget and Q1","detail":"The Ratio of Financing costs to net revenue stream for the Housing Revenue Account was budgeted at 22.20% but shifted to -21.90% in the Q1 estimate, a movement of 44 percentage points. The document does not explain the reason for this material change.","category":"borrowing","matters":"The HRA is a material liability; a swing this large in financing costs indicates a significant change in strategy or assumptions that a lender would need to understand.","figures":"HRA financing ratio: budgeted 22.20%, Q1 estimate -21.90%","quote":"Capital financing costs are interest received, interest paid and the Minimum Revenue Provision. 2.7  22.20% -21.90%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","paper_title":"Appendix A","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51275/51275.pdf","headline":"General fund reserves are forecast to decline by \u00a3194,000","detail":"The Net Movement on General Fund Working Balance shows a full year outturn of (\u00a3194,000), indicating the council will draw down reserves. While modest in amount, it represents the council consuming rather than building financial resilience during the year.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserve depletion constrains future flexibility and suggests recurrent spending is not fully covered by recurrent income, a concern for lenders assessing structural sustainability.","figures":"\u00a3194,000 reduction in general fund balance","quote":"Net Movement on General Fund Working Balance 0 (194) (194)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","paper_title":"Appendix A","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51275/51275.pdf","headline":"Investment income is \u00a3553,000 short of budget at mid-year","detail":"YTD investment income recorded as \u00a3293,000 against a budgeted \u00a3846,000, representing a \u00a3553,000 shortfall. The full year is forecast at \u00a33,485,000 against an annual budget of \u00a33,386,000, but this masks significant first-half underperformance. For the forecast to be met, second-half delivery must accelerate sharply.","category":"income","matters":"Investment income underperformance reduces council financial flexibility and may indicate lower investment yields or lower cash balances than expected\u2014material to lenders assessing returns on cash holdings.","figures":"YTD: budget \u00a3846,000, actual \u00a3293,000, variance \u00a3553,000 shortfall","quote":"Investment Income (846) (293) 553","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","paper_title":"Appendix E","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51279/51279.pdf","headline":"64% of savings target depends on investment income and treasury strategy returns, not cost efficiencies","detail":"The single largest savings item is 'Investment Income/Teasury Management Strategy' at \u00a32,238k of the \u00a33,487k total. This is income-dependent and vulnerable to falling interest rates, not a structural cost saving.","category":"income","matters":"Treasury and investment income targets are inherently volatile and exposed to conditions outside the council's control. Heavy reliance on this measure rather than operational efficiencies creates budget fragility.","figures":"Investment income target: \u00a32,238k out of \u00a33,487k total proposed savings","quote":"Investment Income/Teasury Management Strategy Head of Financial Services (2,238) (2,238)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Finance and Resources Overview and Scrutiny","paper_title":"Appendix E","paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51279/51279.pdf","headline":"Green waste income target is not being achieved; \u00a334k of \u00a3160k now at risk","detail":"The green waste income saving was planned at \u00a3160k but only \u00a3126k is currently on track, with \u00a334k marked as at risk. This is the only item showing delivery risk and suggests the initial income assumption may not materialise.","category":"income","matters":"Shortfalls in savings plans must be replaced elsewhere in the budget or absorbed by reserves. Early slippage on an income target suggests the assumption may be unrealistic.","figures":"Green waste income: \u00a3160k proposed, \u00a3126k on track, \u00a334k at risk","quote":"Green Waste Income Head of Environmental Services (160) (126) (34) 0","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Dacorum","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":false,"headline":"HRA financing costs ratio swings sharply from 22.20% to -21.90% between budget and Q1","lead":"The HRA is a material liability; a swing this large in financing costs indicates a significant change in strategy or assumptions that a lender would need to understand.","also":["21 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-10-06","n_findings":22,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix G","top_paper_url":"http://democracy.dacorum.gov.uk/documents/s51281/51281.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":89,"news_drafts_total":3}}